# Absolute encoder faults on the CN 720's X axis (FANUC alpha-type encoder,
# mturn; mill_x_fanuc.conf, fanuc_sim.txt), each over a drive reset:
# 1. the shaft turns 1.5 turns while the drive is off (battery kept):
#    +15 mm after the reset, still absolute
# 2. the encoder sends a turn count one off (a fault): mturn sees linrev and
#    the encoder disagree, state 3, abs_ok 0
# 3. the battery is out while off: the encoder is un-indexed (mt_ok 0),
#    mturn state 2 (turn count lost), single-turn only; turning past the
#    index makes the encoder valid again but mturn stays lost (its new count
#    is not tied to the machine) until clear (after re-referencing)
# The state reaches LinuxCNC on the drive's spare inputs (mturn.txt):
# in2 = abs_ok, in3 = battery warning.
# 4. a frame error (cable) drops abs_ok; when frames return it loads again
#    (loads since the last reset: 2, after clear and after the error; none
#    at boot, the count was lost)
@args --drive tests/abs/mill_x_fanuc.conf --sim tests/abs/fanuc_sim.txt
lcncscale 10
lcnc 0 0
hv0.sim_upos = 62.83185
run 0.05
reset
run 0.3
linrev0.fb_out
hv0.sim_off_move = 1.5
run 0.05
reset
run 0.3
mturn0.state
linrev0.fb_out
encf0.sim_turn_err = 1
run 0.05
mturn0.state
mturn0.abs_ok
sserial0.in2
encf0.sim_turn_err = 0
encf0.sim_batt = 0
run 0.05
reset
run 0.3
encf0.mt_ok
mturn0.state
mturn0.abs_ok
hv0.sim_turn = 7
run 2
encf0.mt_ok
mturn0.state
mturn0.clear = 1
run 0.01
mturn0.clear = 0
run 0.05
mturn0.state
mturn0.abs_ok
sserial0.in2
encf0.sim_batt_low = 1
run 0.01
sserial0.in3
encf0.sim_batt_low = 0
encf0.sim_fail = 1
run 0.05
mturn0.abs_ok
encf0.sim_fail = 0
run 0.05
mturn0.abs_ok
mturn0.loads
@expect linrev0.fb_out[1] ~ 100 0.001
@expect mturn0.state[1] == 1
@expect linrev0.fb_out[2] ~ 115 0.001
@expect mturn0.state[2] == 3
@expect mturn0.abs_ok[1] == 0
@expect sserial0.in2[-2] == 0
@expect encf0.mt_ok[1] == 0
@expect mturn0.state[3] == 2
@expect mturn0.abs_ok[2] == 0
@expect encf0.mt_ok[2] == 1
@expect mturn0.state[4] == 2
@expect mturn0.state[5] == 1
@expect mturn0.abs_ok[3] == 1
@expect sserial0.in2[-1] == 1
@expect sserial0.in3[-1] == 1
@expect mturn0.abs_ok[4] == 0
@expect mturn0.abs_ok[5] == 1
@expect mturn0.loads == 2
